@meeting train.m9.calder
// Pillar 5 Step 3, M9 tracing (Day 12, Friday): the main version. Calder at the board gives you the pipe kit and shows
// you the water line on the Maps app; the card says "Showers weak on Deck 4". Torres is off on Fridays. Seat M3 plays
// it; her words on the walk are her kind work, flags train.m9.follow.<step>. Head writer W2.
title: The pipe kit
from: Chief Ines Calder
gist: Calder gave you the pipe kit. Read the flow along a line; fine before and low after is your machine.
== lines
calder > you: Here. Your first proper Tier 2 tool. Don't drop it in the manifold.   [gesture]
calder: Clip it on a panel. It reads the flow there. Full, low, very low.
calder: "Showers weak on Deck 4." The card says where it hurts. Not where it starts.
calder: Open your Maps. The water line. Recycler to pumps to valves to your shower.
calder: Read the middle first. Fine there, the trouble's downstream. Low, it's upstream.
calder: Then halve it again. Fine before a machine, low after. That's your machine.
? choice
* Why not start at the showers?   rel:calder+2 flavour:practical
  calder: Because then you read every machine on the ship. Halve it. Always halve it.   [nod]
* Which is the middle?   rel:calder+1 flavour:listen
  calder: The Deck 5 pumps. We'll start there. Together, this once.
* (Clip the kit to your belt)
  calder: Good. Deck 5. Walk.
